<LayoutPage title="Foldster's Projects — Guessr47 (Rewkers)" description="Multiplayer location-guessing for video-game maps">
  <h1>Guessr47.</h1>
  <p class="mono">for Rewkers</p>
  <p class="lede">
    A multiplayer location-guessing game for video-game maps. Host uploads map screenshots with answer pins; players join via short code from chat and guess locations on stream. GeoGuessr for video games.
  </p>

  <h2>The problem.</h2>
  <p>
    Rewkers wanted a stream-side party game that pulled the audience into the broadcast directly — something playable from anywhere with a short join code, not yet-another-overlay watching the host.
  </p>

  <h2>What was built.</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Multiplayer real-time game with sync + async modes</li>
    <li>Twitch OAuth player auth (no separate signup)</li>
    <li>Host-side map upload + answer-pin placement</li>
    <li>Live scoreboard + round timer</li>
    <li>Short code join (paste in chat, players load in)</li>
    <li>Convex backend with realtime subscriptions</li>
    <li>Custom design tokens for brand-matched look</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>The stack.</h2>
  <p class="mono">React / TypeScript / Vite / Convex / Twitch OAuth</p>

  <h2>Live at.</h2>
  <p><a href="https://guessr47.com" target="_blank">guessr47.com</a></p>

  <p class="mono note">case study photos + demo clip + Rewkers quote coming soon.</p>

  <a href="/contact/" class="cta" slot="cta">want something like this for your stream? &rarr;</a>
</LayoutPage>

